From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bonsai-27b-fusion <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Jan 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs(fusion): scope is Bonsai-2-27B, and the stack is green
 for it

The stack only needs to serve Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B, which changes what the KV
defects above mean: the launcher passes -ngl 99 -fa on -c 32768 but no -ctk/-ctv,
so the model runs on the default f16 KV cache, and f16 x f16 measured healthy in
every configuration. So none of those defects apply here. They stay recorded as
upstream / PrismML bug reports, not as blockers.

The one thing that did matter was the build configuration, and since FA_ALL_QUANTS
was flipped on this build dir the target model was re-validated rather than assumed:

  llama-bench -p 512 -n 32 -ngl 99 -fa 1 -r 3
    fusion, FA_ALL_QUANTS=OFF      317.65 prompt / 45.70 gen t/s
    original PrismML, ON           316.44 / 46.13        -> parity inside noise

  coherence, greedy: Paris; 17*23 -> 391; a code request planned correctly

The launcher itself was exercised too, because that is the real entry point:
--list enumerates ROCm0, and --cli forwards a quoted prompt intact and gets a
coherent answer - which doubles as a regression test for the two .bat hazards
(no shift inside a parenthesised block, %2..%9 so quotes survive).

All four PQ2_0 variants were run as well: 43.7-44.2 t/s, coherent, no crashes.

state.json now carries scope and lastValidation, and portStatus says what is true:
complete and green for the target model.
