+
+## 2026-09-19 (scope): this stack exists for Bonsai-2-27B, and it is green
+
+Stated scope: the PrismML fusion only has to serve **Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B**. That
+settles how much the KV defects above matter, and the answer is: not much.
+
+`F:\AI\lm-models\Bonsai-2-27B\start-bonsai.bat` launches with
+
+```text
+-ngl 99 -fa on -c 32768 --jinja --cache-prompt --cont-batching --parallel 1
+```
+
+and **does not pass `-ctk`/`-ctv`**, so the model runs on the **default f16 KV
+cache**. f16 x f16 is the one combination that measured healthy in every
+configuration tested today:
+
+| | FA_ALL_QUANTS ON | OFF |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| f16 x f16 | 6.9921 | 6.9921 |
+
+So none of the KV defects apply to this model, and they are recorded as upstream /
+PrismML bug reports rather than as blockers here. The one thing that did matter is
+the build configuration, and it is settled: **FA_ALL_QUANTS=OFF**.
+
+### Re-validation after the build-config change
+
+Changing the build option changed the binary the launcher points at, so the target
+model was re-measured rather than assumed.
+
+`llama-bench -p 512 -n 32 -ngl 99 -fa 1 -r 3`, Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-PQ2_0:
+
+| build | prompt tok/s | generation tok/s |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| fusion, FA_ALL_QUANTS=OFF | **317.65** | **45.70** |
+| original PrismML, FA_ALL_QUANTS=ON | 316.44 | 46.13 |
+
+Parity inside run-to-run noise, as expected: f16 KV selects the same instance
+either way.
+
+Coherence, greedy, `-fa on -ngl 99`:
+
+```text
+"The capital of France is"               -> [Start thinking] ... Final: Paris. [End thinking]  Paris
+"what is 17 * 23?"                       -> 17*20=340, 17*3=51 total 391
+"Write a Python function that reverses a string..." -> plans the function and the comment
+```
+
+All three correct, including the arithmetic.
+
+### The launcher itself
+
+Both branches of `start-bonsai.bat` were exercised, since that file is the actual
+entry point:
+
+```text
+start-bonsai.bat --list                       -> ROCm0: AMD Radeon RX 6900 XT (16368 MiB, 16226 MiB free)
+start-bonsai.bat --cli -p "The capital ..."   -> prompt forwarded intact, model answers coherently
+```
+
+The second one is the regression test for the two .bat hazards recorded in the
+skill: no `shift` inside a parenthesised block, and `%2..%9` rather than `%~2..` so
+quotes survive. A quoted prompt arriving intact means both hold.
+
+The banner in the header was stale (`build b2-c6fbb78`) and now records the code
+commit and the FA_ALL_QUANTS=OFF configuration.
+
+Records: `temp_clean_later/bench-results/bonsai-revalidate`.
+
+### All four Bonsai variants
+
+The launcher defaults to one of them, but four are on disk and all are the same
+format, so they were all run (greedy, `-ngl 99 -fa 1 -c 2048`):
+
+| model | rc | generation tok/s | answer |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-PQ2_0 | 0 | 43.7 | plans, answers Paris |
+| Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-Uncensored-Heretic-PQ2_0 | 0 | 44.0 | same |
+| TERNARY-BONSAI-2-27B-DERISKED-PQ2_0 | 0 | 44.0 | same |
+| Bonsai-2-27B-PQ2_0-CRACK | 0 | 44.2 | same |
+
+No crashes, no format differences, no variant-specific behaviour.
